{{afc comment|1=definitely notable[[User:Immanuelle|'''Immanuel'''le]] ❤️💚💙 [[User_talk:Immanuelle|(talk to the cutest Wikipedian)]] 06:21, 3 November 2023 (UTC)}}
{{ill|Tashima Shrine|ja| Toggle the table of contents 田島神社|simple|6=draft}} is a shrine situated on {{ill|Kabe Island|ja|加部島|ceb|Kabe_Shima_(pulo_sa_Hapon,_Saga-ken)}} in [[Yobuko]] Town, [[Karatsu]] City, [[Saga Prefecture]].<ref>{{Cite book |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=QNw5D3Br8BoC&newbks=0&printsec=frontcover&dq=Tashima+Shrine&q=Tashima+Shrine&hl=en |title=The Japan Magazine: A Representative Monthly of Things Japanese |date=1928 |publisher=Japan magazine Company |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |last=Hall |first=Jessica |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=bmiYUKjEBMoC&newbks=0&printsec=frontcover&dq=Tashima+Shrine&q=Tashima+Shrine&hl=en |title=The Deepest Edge |date=2003 |publisher=Signet |isbn=978-0-451-20796-8 |language=en}}</ref> It is located in the area known as [[Matsurokoku]], which is believed to be the first land of the mainland of [[Wakoku]] as per [[Wajinden]] records. It is an important point for safe sea crossings to the continent, and has received significant orders from the central government since ancient times.

In earlier times, it was called 'Tajima Niimasu Kaminoyashiro'. It is the only [[Myojin Taisha]] in [[Hizen Province]], and was previously classified as [[Modern system of ranked Shinto shrines|Kokuhei Chusha]] due to renovations during the [[Meiji period]]. Currently, it is a [[beppyo shrine]] of the [[Association of Shinto Shrines]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=別表神社とは？御朱印めぐりに参考になる「別表神社一覧」とマップ {{!}} 開運戦隊ゴシュインジャー |url=https://jinja-gosyuin.com/beppyou/ |access-date=2023-04-02 |website=jinja-gosyuin.com}}</ref> It is associated with Sayohime Matsuura, whose poem was written by Okura Yamanoue, and is said to be the original shrine (roots) of [[Munakata Taisha]].

It is a Munakata shrine<ref>{{Cite book |last=Kalland |first=Arne |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=wp4xhRXsARcC&newbks=0&printsec=frontcover&pg=PA47&dq=Tashima+Shrine&hl=en |title=Fishing Villages in Tokugawa, Japan |date=1995-01-01 |publisher=University of Hawaii Press |isbn=978-0-8248-1632-2 |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite book |last=Rots |first=Aike P. |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=pcjZDwAAQBAJ&newbks=0&printsec=frontcover&pg=PT104&dq=Tashima+Shrine&hl=en |title=Sacred Heritage in Japan |last2=Teeuwen |first2=Mark |date=2020-04-02 |publisher=Routledge |isbn=978-1-000-04563-5 |language=en}}</ref>

