<ref name=kelsey1981-miwasan-setsuwa>{{harvp|Kelsey|1981}} explains that narratives of a god-human intermarriages are designated {{nihongo|''shinkon shinwa''|神婚神話|extra="myths of marriages to deities"}}, and tales where the male spouse is divine are subcategorized as {{nihongo|''Miwasan-kei setsuwa''|三輪山型説話|extra="stories of the Mt. Miwa pattern"}}, p. 219. He lists examples of the tale group under "Appendix 2: Stories of ''shinkon''", and his story 33,  is "The Mt. Miwa Story" where Ōmononushi is followed using the thread, p. 232.</ref>

